        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Lima</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1535 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a> founded the city in 1535 as the City of Kings, on land that had belonged to the local lord Taulichusco, in a valley long held by the Ichma polity.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">In the valleys of the Chillón, Rímac and Lurín rivers on the desert coast of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, overlooking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-ocean">Pacific Ocean</a>, with the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/callao">Callao</a> beside it.</span></div>
